 "title": "Official Website for Norton County Kansas - Appraiser",
 "text": "Official Website for Norton County Kansas - Appraiser\nSkip to main content\nView Alerts X Alert\n🗳️2026 GENERAL ELECTION🗳️ VOTING DEADLINES 🔴OCTOBER 20, 2026: EARLY IN-PERSON VOTING BEGINS ⚪OCTOBER 27, 2026: DEADLINE FOR VOTERS TO APPLY FOR ADVANCE BALLOTS TO BE MAILED 🔵NOVEMBER 2, 2026: EARLY IN-PERSON VOTING ENDS @ NOON 🔴NOVEMBER 3, 2026: GENERAL ELECTION 🗳️ POLLS OPEN 7:00AM-7:00PM🗳️ ⚪NOVEMBER 6, 2026: DEADLINE FOR RECEIPT OF ADVANCE BALLOTS POSTMARKED ON OR BEFORE ELECTION DAY\n‹ 1 of 2 Alerts ›\nWelcome To\nNorton County\nKansas\nSearch\nOur Government\nAbout Norton County\nBoard of County Commissioners\nCounty Clerk\nElections Home Page\n2026 Elections\nTreasurer\nRegister of Deeds\nCounty Attorney\nSheriff's Office\nDistrict Court\nDepartments\nEmergency Management\nHealth\nEmergency Medical Service (EMS)\nAppraiser\nRoad and Bridge\nNoxious Weeds\nSolid Waste\nCivic Organizations\nNorton County Community Foundation\nNorton American Legion #63\nNorton American Legion Auxiliary\nNorton Eagles Lodge\nNorton Farmer's Market\nNorton Lions Club\nNorton Rotary Club\nCities\nNorton, Kansas\nAlmena, Kansas\nLenora, Kansas\nClayton, Kansas\nEdmond, Kansas\nJobs\nDeputy Appraiser\nMindy Harting\nWork: 785-877-5700\nmindy@nortoncountyks.gov\nAppraiser\nORKA Website\nCounty Appraiser FAQ\nProperty Valuation Appeal Guide\nPersonal Property Assessment Form\nCurrent Job Postings\nGeneral Information\nStaff Directory\nLocation\n105 South Kansas Avenue\nCourthouse 2nd Floor\nNorton,\nKS\n67654\nGet Directions\nHours\nMonday through Friday\n8:00am - 12:00pm & 1:00pm - 5:00pm\nAppraiser\nHome >\nDepartments >\nAppraiser\nFunction of Department\nThe Appraiser's Department is responsible for determining the fair market value of all assessable properties. The appraiser analyzes trends in sales prices, construction costs, and rents to estimate such value. Real property and personal property is appraised as of January 1 every year. Partially complete new construction is appraised based upon its percentage of completion as of January 1. Market value (what a willing buyer and willing seller would agree to) is the basis of value for most real property except agricultural land. Agricultural land is appraised on the basis of its productivity and a formula determined by Kansas Constitution, statutes, and state guidelines. Most personal property (except business, machinery equipment, RVs, etc.) is also appraised at market value.\nBuying a Home?\nThe County Appraiser is required to value real property, excluding land devoted to agriculture use, at fair market value. If your purchase is an open-market transaction, it may be used as a comparable property to value itself and like properties.\nA calculation that can be used to estimate your property taxes after your purchase is:\nPurchase Price X Assessment Rate X Mill Rate = Estimated Taxes\n069 NT 2025 Legal Notice for trend.pdf\n069 NT 2024 Legal Notice for trend.doc\n069 NT 2023 Legal Notice for trend.doc\n090 NT 2026 Legal Notice for trend.pdf\ndc-notice-to-public-publishingpdf.pdf\nORKA Website\nContact Info\n105 South Kansas Ave\nNorton KS 67654\n785-877-5710\nWebsite By EvoGov",
